sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-20: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.51" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.508"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.55"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "A morphospace distance from fossils to embryos versus living adults is a concrete criterion, and it can be built for a few skeletal systems that have both fossil scans and developmental series. Most clades lack that joint coverage, and side-branch fossils are an imperfect stand-in for ancestors. The comparison is informative where the landmarks exist and is not a general test across extinct life." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Place fossil adults and the embryos and adults of their living relatives in one morphospace and test whether the fossils fall closer to the embryos than to the living adults. The claim is confirmed if stem fossils are repeatedly more embryo-like than their living adult relatives, and refuted if they are as close, or closer, to the living adults across well-sampled clades." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Fossil adults and embryos of descendants are rarely landmarked in the same coordinate system.", "A stem fossil is a side branch, so resemblance to an embryo need not mean it preserves the ancestor's adult form.", "Early-acting changes, which the claim itself allows, remove the predicted resemblance and make a negative result ambiguous." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-20--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-20 by Grok 4.7: 0.6" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
